# The +1/+0 is the hone counter's, not an ability of the Equipment (CR 122.1j; the ruling: "even if the Equipment loses some of
# its abilities, each hone counter will still grant +1/+0"). Paradise Mantle, with the hone counter Dwalin's entering put on it, is
# equipped to Dwalin on turn 5. Turn 7: Bot1 activates the Mantle's equip ability to move it to Ornithopter, and Bot2 flashes in
# Tishana's Tidebinder to counter that ability, so the Mantle stays on Dwalin and loses all its abilities while the Tidebinder
# remains (Dwalin, which could tap for mana with the Mantle's granted ability on turn 5, no longer can). Dwalin is still 3/1;
# attacking, it puts a second hone counter on the Mantle, which still counts: Dwalin strikes for 4.

